{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_57k4nb32khp4szb2wypgdunadatgvmmc4655tjlnlw6mu26tfgea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four gates pass.\n\n## What the library is\n\nThe entire C library is one translation unit (`driver.c`, 50 lines): `void driver(int)` builds `house_t { int floors; int bedrooms; double bathrooms; }`, sets `floors` from the argument, hard-codes `bedrooms = 3` / `bathrooms = 2.0`, `memcpy`s it into a `char[16]`, and hex-dumps those 16 bytes plus a newline via a `static` helper. No module was left untranslated — confirmed by an empty `nm -D` diff, not by inspection.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| gate | status |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo check` (incl. all test targets) | 0 errors, 0 warnings |\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — symbol parity | empty diff; only libc/libgcc undefined symbols |\n| Phase B — 19/19 `CONFIGS.md` rows | pass, 0 unchecked |\n| Phase C — 10/10 `ERRORS.md` rows + generic sweep (11 cases) | pass, 0 unchecked |\n| Every feature combo × both profiles | 4/4 pairs pass |\n\nNo divergence was found, so `src/lib.rs` is unchanged from the pristine translation.\n\n## Two harness bugs that were faking results\n\nWorth flagging, because in both cases the suite *reported* something untrue:\n\n1. **`cargo test` silently tested a stale `.so`.** No test target links the `cdylib` (tests `dlopen` it), so cargo never rebuilds it. A deliberate `bedrooms = 4` mutant **survived the entire suite** — the tests kept loading the previous build. Fixed with an `assert_fresh` mtime guard that aborts with a rebuild hint, plus an explicit `cargo build` per configuration in the runner script.\n2. **libtest's own output leaked into the fd-1 capture.** Redirecting fd 1 is process-global, but libtest writes progress lines from other threads and Rust's `stdout` `LineWriter` can flush a newline-less fragment *after* the redirect installs. Seven Phase B cases \"failed\" on payloads that were actually byte-identical. Fixed with `harness = false` + sequential `run_suite`, and draining `std::io::stdout()` before each redirect.\n\n## Sensitivity evidence\n\nRather than trusting green checkmarks, I injected 9 bugs into the Rust: wrong constants, sign-extension in the hex printer, `%02X`/`%x` format changes, dropped newline, off-by-one loop bound, swapped field order — **all killed**. `#[repr(C, packed)]` survived, and I verified that's an *equivalent* mutant rather than a gap: `{i32, i32, f64}` has no padding, so size (16) and offsets (0/4/8) are identical and only `align_of` differs, which is unobservable through an API that only `memcpy`s the struct.\n\nThe sign-extension mutant is the useful one — it's killed only by the high-byte-pattern rows (C7/C8/C10) and passes every small-positive input, which is exactly why `CONFIGS.md` enumerates byte-pattern classes instead of calling `driver` once.\n\n## One judgement call to be aware of\n\n`ERRORS.md` has **no true error rows**: grepping the C for `return`/`assert`/`NULL`/range checks/`MIN`/`MAX`/`malloc` yields zero hits. `driver` is `void`, validates nothing, and accepts all 2³² `int` values, so there is no error code or sentinel to compare. Phase C therefore asserts *identical disposition* (same 33 output bytes, same acceptance, no abort) across hostile inputs — including out-of-range enum-like ints, `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`, and unsigned values above `INT_MAX`. I deliberately did **not** invent \"null pointer to `driver`\" or \"oversized length\" rows, since its sole parameter is a by-value `int`; those generic boundaries are discharged where the library's only pointer and length actually live, inside `static print_hex`, which is provably unreachable externally (asserted via `nm -D` and a failing `dlsym` on both objects).\n\nArtifacts: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `run_all_feature_combos.sh`, and `tests/{common/mod.rs, phase_b_configs.rs, phase_c_errors.rs}`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1279,"cache_read_input_tokens":95329,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1279,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fab0a299-dd8c-46ac-bd25-b0d4e14c546c","uuid":"b4e34d18-b2f5-4757-ae79-d225ec2e424f","timestamp":"2026-08-28T16:43:01.573Z"}
